{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803749-can-demon-survive-losing-the-paradise-lost-bits","id":803749,"title":"Can Demon Survive Losing The Paradise Lost Bits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T08:06:48-08:00","id":803749,"title":"Can Demon Survive Losing The Paradise Lost Bits?","content":"So I'm a pro-government, god-believing wimp, and I like a lot of parts of Demon. These don't, however, include the parts where the game decides to really invest in the whole &quot;eternal conflict between the dictatorial God-Machine and freedom-loving Demons&quot; bit. It feels like most of the game works fine with the God-Machine taking a somewhat more Promethean Principle-type approach (serving as an ineffable cosmic force working towards an unknown goal of unknown worthiness) while Demons struggle to balance their new existences with their still relevant vestiges of their time as an Angel. That said, the game devotes so much time to the cold war between Demons and the God-Machine, to the idea of the Demon as one who &quot;rejected the primacy of the God-Machine and defected to the Human race&quot; (Heirs to Hell, pg. 16), that I worry I'm basically lobotomizing the game. Is this the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","name":"Crosswords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:18:06-08:00","id":803752,"title":"","content":"I suppose that without an active conflict then there'd be nothing to drive the angst. Everyone would be settling down or colonising in some respect. Without the oppression of the God Machine there's nothing to struggle against. The Machine is, I feel, enough of an Outside Context Problem to be divorced from ideas of either government or loving god. It should be fought because its activity is erasure and enslavement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:39:54-08:00","id":803763,"title":"","content":"Demon's an espionage game. What you're proposing isn't just a thematic shift, it's a complete rejection of a solid half of the game's premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:52:20-08:00","id":803778,"title":"","content":"Much of Demon's mechanics require the &quot;threat overhead&quot; of the God-Machine. The themes of a spy under cover are one. The justification for Cover, and thus Compromise checks is another. There needs to be <i>some</i> explanation for why Demon's keep their heads down, after all.<br /> <br /> If you want to downplay the Tyranny of the Machine, you could play up its inscrutability: The God-Machine has plans, and Demons have decided to go their own way. They are still leery of drawing their former (Master?Father?Maker?Controller?)'s attention, because even if benign, it is still the G-M making the decisions, not the Demon.<br /> <br /> Less &quot;I'm going to enslave/recycle you vs FREEDOM!&quot; and more &quot;Let me include you in my plan vs Let me make my own choices, good or ill&quot;. Changes the feel from Slave-Master to Parent (well meaning or overprotective as you decide).<br /> <hr /><br /> Addendum: I'm honestly curious to see if a non-G-M reason can be found. It would be useful in justifying minimal rules changes in the &quot;Unchained-run, otherwise stock fantasy&quot; setting I'm working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-08-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:26:40-08:00","id":803827,"title":"","content":"The thing about the Machine is just that. It's cold and calculating. It doesn't sends hunter angels after the Unchained because of some malign vendetta for having defied it, the simple truth is that this happens out of pragmatism. Angels, fallen or otherwise, are resources to it. Which bear getting recycled. It doesn't has infinite resources. Pesky thing called Entropy getting in the way.<br /> <br /> At least one of my chronicles is gonna end with a Saboteur agency fucking up an infrastructure that basically prevented 117 different types of Omega-Delta End of the World Cataclysmic Event because &quot;MACHINE BAD! FREEDOM GOOD!&quot; And with said demons surviving on a post-apocalyptic wasteland to their very literal Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:29:57-08:00","id":803830,"title":"","content":"Alright, it's pretty clear from the responses that it is at the very least a very likely massive shift. I hope it's not a problem if I still engage you folks despite that, and that this post won't be too long.<br /> ---<br /> To Malkydel, on Angst and the Risk of Diminishing the Action:<br /> If anything, I would say that the angst becomes more personal. If the GM is not automatically in a position of wanting you dead, then you lose the automatic motivation for opposing the GM, that of &quot;mere&quot; self-preservation. As you say, you could well settle down to a degree, but the GM is still operating. More importantly, you know it's still working. It's still building and tearing down, killing as it sees fit to pursue its unknown goals. Are you, a fallen angel who still has some shred of power, comfortable just sitting around while that happens? I think the Agendas line up wonderfully with the most likely answers.<br /> ---<br /> To atamajakki, on Losing Espionage:<br /> If the events of the last few years have demonstrated anything, it's that espionage isn't limited to one's activity enemies. The USA still isn't at war with Germany, but we bugged their Chancellor's phone. Not to mention, just because the GM is tolerating a Demon live quietly in an apartment doesn't mean that Demon will do so. An Inquisitor is going to want to know what the GM is doing outside, a Saboteur is going to want the GM dead, and an Integrator won't be interested in just being &quot;tolerated&quot;.<br /> ---<br /> To Vent0, on the Threat Overhead:<br /> It might take some mechanical rejiggering, but you could probably use the God-Machine's general tendency towards surveillance and micro-managing to justify Cover and such. The God-Machine might find a Demon cleaning up the streets in its Demonic Form to be too large of an uncontrolled variable to justify keeping him around. Maybe make it more of a DEFCON situation than a flat targeted/non-targeted? The core-book seems to have the conditions for something like that, though it lets you choose one rather than providing a kind of organized progression (which makes sense).<br /> <br /> As for non-God Machine related reasons for keeping Cover and Compromise, crossover can be useful. The other gamelines have plenty of secret agent-types who might be interested in the village accountant actually being a rogue robot agent. It's not a unique situation, though that would be more fun, but it could lead to some enjoyable Ruroni Kenshin-esque storylines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","user":"Crosswords","date":".  I decided to revise my response to Vent0, since there were some very stupid things. 01-08-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","name":"Crosswords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:10:39-08:00","id":804046,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Idea I just thought of to justify Compromise rolls: Demonic messing around with reality (the Demonic Form, Exploits) is <b>bad</b> for said reality. The Machine knows the right time and place for it's powers, and actively cleans up after itself, but Demons, metaphorically speaking, trash the house like only the truly ignorant can, then leave before picking up after themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T12:26:05-08:00","id":805397,"title":"","content":"You could change your perspective on the god machine to some extent. In the next game I'm going to run set in Detroit. The god machine is a force for &quot;good&quot; or at least most people might think so given the alternative. where good is sort of the skewed how many thousands are worth sacrificing for billions. The G-M is actually trying to keep us alive and advance us. Demons have kicked the G-M out of Detroit, that's why it's gone down hill, the monsters are running the show. Recently the G-M is making progress in regaining control of this hellscape.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller guide gives a few different ways to play demon including some where &quot;you've won, now you have to deal with maintaining your hell&quot;. The intro story discusses a case where the GM is observing a Demon living his life out in his hell because this observation is allowing the GM to capture many other Demons. Basically STG might be a good resource for you here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:08:36-08:00","id":805429,"title":"","content":"Demon suffers if you mute the conflict between the Unchained and the God-Machine. As xenoterracide says, though, what it <i>can</i> do fine is render that conflict ambiguous and complicated. There's a reason Integrators are presented as often enjoying not just an uneasy peace but an ambiguous cooperation with the other agendas: the God-Machine isn't unified in its outlook. It has many parts with different priorities and methods, some of which a demon would likely find more objectionable than others (and which those would be might vary from demon to demon). There are angels with whom deals can be struck. There are projects working at cross-purposes.<br /> <br /> The espionage angle comes in there, then, in maintaining your Cover in general to avoid being exposed to general God-Machine agents, whose usual policy might lead them to cooperate with your enemies against you, while getting in to see the agents of the Machine who might be more sympathetic, and carefully striking deals with them to further your goals and set back your enemies'. And, of course, in never being entirely sure when you can rely on your allies and when they might find it more advantageous to turn on you.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's at odds with the default tone of the game at all; it certainly lines up well with my image of Demon. The Machine has no innate moral qualities, positive or negative. It's simply a runaway process. If no one steps up to check and guide it, it will act amorally to a general detriment. Simply demolishing it indiscriminately would also be catastrophic. In order to manage the system, demons dance on the line between insider and outsider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:02:57-08:00","id":805611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/803749-can-demon-survive-losing-the-paradise-lost-bits?p=805397#post805397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storyteller guide gives a few different ways to play demon including some where &quot;you've won, now you have to deal with maintaining your hell&quot;. The intro story discusses a case where the GM is observing a Demon living his life out in his hell because this observation is allowing the GM to capture many other Demons. Basically STG might be a good resource for you here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still working my way through it, but it's good to hear there's still good stuff ahead. I kind of skip around with .pdfs, probably to the detriment of my understanding. The Hell section really was right up my alley, and certainly got me thinking about just how interesting Demon interactions with just the general mortal community could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","name":"Crosswords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:41:37-08:00","id":806285,"title":"","content":"What I really love about DtD is that it has a ton of thematic sliders, so I don't think you'll lobotomize the game by focusing on the parts of the game you like. I think there's a ton of ambiguity about the nature of the God-Machine already in the text. It preserves life on earth by deflecting asteroids, and it blunts the effects of omnicidal natural events. Heck, that's what the Agendas are about! &quot;We broke away from the God-Machine, and now we have to decide how we feel about that.&quot; Not everyone takes the Saboteur perspective. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One thing you could do to reduce the level of antagonism is to replace Hunter Angels with Recruitment Angels like Alexandra Fairchild on page 219 of the Corebook. When the God-Machine becomes aware of your demons through embeds and exploits, the demon's old comrades come to see what they're up to, and how they're adjusting to life on the outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 01-11-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}